.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/17/FB_WVUvsCincinnati_Oct17_2026_AM-29.jpeg"><media:title>West Virginia fans and players sing "Take Me Home, Country Roads" after West Virginia's win against Cincinnati on Oct. 17, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/17/FB_WVUvsCincinnati_Oct17_2026_AM-29.jpeg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 07:45:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59549</s:story_id></item><item><title>Countdown to Kickoff: Impressive Ground Attacks on Display Today</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/17/football-countdown-to-kickoff-impressive-ground-attacks-on-display-today</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/17/football-countdown-to-kickoff-impressive-ground-attacks-on-display-today</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Milan Puskar Stripe the Stadium for a game played in Morgantown in 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/13/milan_puskar_stadium3__9-13-25_by_dan_friend__TLtKp.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Two of the top rushing teams in the Big 12 Conference will meet at high noon today when West Virginia faces Cincinnati in a Homecoming contest at Milan Puskar Stadium.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/13/milan_puskar_stadium3__9-13-25_by_dan_friend__TLtKp.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/13/milan_puskar_stadium3__9-13-25_by_dan_friend__TLtKp.jpg"><media:title>Milan Puskar Stripe the Stadium for a game played in Morgantown in 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/13/milan_puskar_stadium3__9-13-25_by_dan_friend__TLtKp.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 07:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59550</s:story_id></item><item><title>Big Second Half Pushes Mountaineers Past Kentucky</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/mens-soccer-big-second-half-pushes-mountaineers-past-kentucky</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/mens-soccer-big-second-half-pushes-mountaineers-past-kentucky</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Isaac Scheer takes a shot for WVU men's soccer against Kentucky" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/16/MSOC_vKentucky_10162026-23.jpeg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 24 West Virginia University men's soccer team picked up its first victory in its last five matches with a dominant 4-0 win over Kentucky, Friday evening at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium. The Mountaineers improve to 6-2-4 and 2-1-2 in the Sun Belt while the Wildcats fall to 1-8-3 and 1-3-1 in conference play.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/16/MSOC_vKentucky_10162026-23.jpeg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/16/MSOC_vKentucky_10162026-23.jpeg"><media:title>Isaac Scheer takes a shot for WVU men's soccer against Kentucky</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/16/MSOC_vKentucky_10162026-23.jpeg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:01:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59553</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Down Cincinnati in Four Sets Friday Evening</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/volleyball-mountaineers-down-cincinnati-in-four-sets-friday-evening</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/volleyball-mountaineers-down-cincinnati-in-four-sets-friday-evening</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU Volleyball team sings Country Roads after defeating Cincinnati in four sets on Oct. 16" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/16/DSC08813__1_.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. - The West Virginia University volleyball team (10-7, 3-4 Big 12) defeated Cincinnati, 3-1, on Friday evening at Hope Coliseum, earning its first victory over the Bearcats since 2023 by set scores of 25-21, 25-14, 27-29 and 25-19.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/16/DSC08813__1_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/16/DSC08813__1_.jpg"><media:title>WVU Volleyball team sings Country Roads after defeating Cincinnati in four sets on Oct. 16</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/16/DSC08813__1_.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:55:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59552</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Fall to UCF Friday Afternoon</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/womens-soccer-mountaineers-fall-to-ucf-friday-afternoon</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/16/womens-soccer-mountaineers-fall-to-ucf-friday-afternoon</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Tyler Clyburn passes the ball during a game at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium." src=